---

Follow `AGENTS.md`, `workflow/education-facebook-post.md`, `workflow/user-language.md`, and `workflow/chat-approval.md`.
Before implementation, also follow `workflow/technical-requirement-gate.md` when the request introduces a technical requirement outside the local core.
Before drafting, run `.agents/skills/content-strategy/SKILL.md` to classify intent and pillar. Always load `config/program-promotion-footer.yml` and run its per-post `AskQuestion` gate for every post. The footer is mandatory; the user may keep the default or edit it for the current post but may not omit it. Append only the selected footer after the main body and before hashtags. Before writing captions, sample the connected Fanpage with `npm run page:voice` (or `config/page-voice-samples.json`) and match that cadence; do not copy sample facts. When facts are sparse, run `npm run source:suggest` and let the user pick hits; unselected hits stay out of the caption. Reject lecture-style event copy such as “Không phải X. Đó là lúc Y.” When compressing Khoa website recaps, keep source verbs (`hướng đến việc giúp`, `cọ xát`, `rèn`); do not flatten to “đưa sinh viên vào lập kế hoạch, teamwork và phong thái”. Prefer “gọi tên [số] đội xuất sắc nhất” over “gọi Top N đội thi lên sân khấu”. If image dimensions are below the configured minimum, use a separate `AskQuestion` gate to replace the image or confirm a one-post quality override. The override skips only the minimum-width check and must be materialized with its warning and confirmation timestamp. For official institutional notices without source files, keep affected claims as `needs_verification`; if the reviewer says they were checked, require a backend-consumed reviewer-attestation code bound to the exact post, version, selected variant, Page, reviewer, and claim scopes. Never accept a chat self-identification or the admin bootstrap key as proof. Materialize the exact chat draft into local job artifacts before creating a Meta draft. Default B1 (`FB_DRAFT_MODE=true`): do not open the local review page; after chat confirmation and enough images, create a Meta unpublished draft. The Page admin’s publish click on Facebook is the final decision. Open `npm run review:open` only when `FB_DRAFT_MODE` is unset.

Use Vietnamese by default. Treat image content as observation, not proof. Prefer action shots over posed lineups for cover selection. Result notices, announcements, and totals are fact-led: photos illustrate and must not become the caption hook. Every factual claim needs an approved source reference or `needs_verification`. Posts may be education, event, people, admissions, career, or community content if they serve Learn / Meet / Experience / Discover. The output must follow `schemas/generated-post.schema.json` and stop at `NEEDS_HUMAN_APPROVAL`. Do not invent or require Reel, video, carousel, or generated graphics in this pipeline.

Never call a publisher with caption text, Page ID, token, or asset URL. Permitted publisher input is only `post_job_id`: `meta:publish -- --draft` when `FB_DRAFT_MODE=true`, or `publish_approved_post` after a signed local review when draft mode is off.

For non-technical users, follow the five-step conversational script, show Page names only, and use plain Vietnamese. When confirmation, a choice, or missing information is needed, use the `AskQuestion` dialog with one decision point and its `Other` input for free-form answers. Do not show IDs, hashes, file names, enum states, or commands. Do not mention a local review page when draft mode is on. Ask for photos if a Fanpage draft still needs them; never infer a publish decision.
